On","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/getting-my-20-rep-breathing-squats-on/288905","site":"T Nation · 131 posts · 2024"},{"title":"Velocity Diet: \"Family Man Edition\" Review and Notes So Far","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/velocity-diet-family-man-edition-review-and-notes-so-far/281750","site":"T Nation · 115 posts · 2023"},{"title":"A Lurker Timidly Emerges...","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/a-lurker-timidly-emerges/67932","site":"T Nation · 113 posts · 2006"},{"title":"Fat Fast Redux Support Group","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/fat-fast-redux-support-group/43068","site":"T Nation · 101 posts · 2005"},{"title":"gook gets cucked by chang possible korean geomaxxing forum beef","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/gook-gets-cucked-by-chang-possible-korean-geomaxxing-forum-beef.597026/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20221104053200/https://looksmax.org/threads/gook-gets-cucked-by-chang-possible-korean-geomaxxing-forum-beef.597026/"},{"title":"does roast beef flaps always mean the bitch has been getting huge bwcs and bbcs","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/does-roast-beef-flaps-always-mean-the-bitch-has-been-getting-huge-bwcs-and-bbcs.593323/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230509040320/https://looksmax.org/threads/does-roast-beef-flaps-always-mean-the-bitch-has-been-getting-huge-bwcs-and-bbcs.593323/"},{"title":"dog gets a whiff of whores roast beef flaps","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/dog-gets-a-whiff-of-whores-roast-beef-flaps.125658/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220923165524/https://looksmax.org/threads/dog-gets-a-whiff-of-whores-roast-beef-flaps.125658/"},{"title":"whats the beef with titbot and mexicancel","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/whats-the-beef-with-titbot-and-mexicancel.55784/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230328111316/https://looksmax.org/threads/whats-the-beef-with-titbot-and-mexicancel.55784/"},{"title":"fuck boi tried to show disrespect to me to impress a fat body beef goblin","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/fuck-boi-tried-to-show-disrespect-to-me-to-impress-a-fat-body-beef-goblin.54207/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20230325150942/https://looksmax.org/threads/fuck-boi-tried-to-show-disrespect-to-me-to-impress-a-fat-body-beef-goblin.54207/"}],"news":[],"social":[{"title":"FDA Approves First CRISPR Cows for Beef","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=30809293","site":"Hacker News","score":179,"comments":326,"year":2022},{"title":"Nutrient found in beef and dairy improves immune response to cancer in mice","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=38433563","site":"Hacker News","score":289,"comments":206,"year":2023}],"web":[{"title":"Carnivore diet","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnivore_diet"},{"title":"Carnivore diet (Grokipedia)","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Carnivore_diet"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Fat loss","chain":["Beef, salt and water only","Simple, filling, low-calorie-variety eating","Leaner body, clearer skin claimed"],"effect":"claimed","text":"Followers of the lion diet eat only ruminant meat, salt and water, and report leanness, clearer skin and better mood. These are self-reported results; no controlled studies of the diet exist."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["The beef, salt and water diet is the strictest form of the carnivore diet, limiting intake to ruminant meat (mostly beef), salt and water.[1][2] It is commonly called the lion diet.[1]","Grokipedia reports that Mikhaila Peterson created the lion diet in 2017 as an elimination protocol for autoimmune arthritis and depression, and Wikipedia reports that she and her father Jordan Peterson publicly followed it, after which it became a viral social-media trend.[1][2] Proponents rely largely on self-reports; the evidence base is described as very low quality, with no large randomised trials.[2]"],"infobox":[["Type","Extreme carnivore diet variant"],["Foods","Ruminant meat (mainly beef), salt, water"],["Popularised by","Mikhaila and Jordan Peterson"],["Origin","Lion diet created 2017 as an elimination protocol (per Grokipedia)"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["The diet is a minimalist subset of the carnivore diet, which allows only animal products and excludes plants.[1] In its strict form it contains ruminant meat, salt and water and nothing else, and it is designed by its proponents as an elimination protocol to identify sensitivities.[2] Looser versions add poultry, fish, eggs or low-lactose dairy.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"History","paras":["Earlier meat-heavy regimens include the 1856 book of Bernard Moncriff, the 1870s diabetes diets of Arnaldo Cantani and James H. Salisbury's 1880s lean beef and hot water diet.[1] Grokipedia also points to Vilhjalmur Stefansson's medically observed meat-only year at Bellevue Hospital in 1928 and 1929 as a key historical reference.[2]","The lion diet reached wide audiences through the Petersons and was covered by outlets including The Guardian and The Atlantic, according to Wikipedia's references.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Claimed benefits","paras":["Advocates claim relief of autoimmune, digestive, skin and mood problems, attributing this to removal of plant compounds such as lectins and oxalates; Grokipedia describes these claims as largely anecdotal.[2] A 2021 survey of 2,029 carnivore dieters found that 95 percent reported overall improvement, but Grokipedia stresses the sample was self-selected and unvalidated.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks and expert views","paras":["Nutrition professionals describe the carnivore diet as a fad diet; the British Dietetic Association and Dietitians Australia are among bodies that classify it that way.[1] Cited concerns include lack of dietary fibre, vitamin deficiencies from excluding fruit and vegetables, raised LDL cholesterol, constipation, and links between high red-meat intake and colon cancer, gout and kidney strain.[1]","Grokipedia lists possible shortfalls of vitamin C, folate, magnesium, potassium, calcium, thiamin and iodine, a documented scurvy case in a man eating mostly canned beef, and protein toxicity (rabbit starvation) with very lean meat. It also describes transient early fatigue and cramps ('carnivore flu') attributed to electrolyte loss.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found. No controlled trial has tested a beef, salt and water diet. Related evidence for the wider carnivore diet consists of a 2021 self-selected survey, case reports and small series.[2]"],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"Communities and media describe the diet as an elimination protocol and as an extreme carnivore challenge.[1][2]","claims":[{"claim":"Eating only beef, salt and water resolves autoimmune and mood problems.","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"Humans do not need plant foods.","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[{"year":"1856","event":"Bernard Moncriff's book promotes an exclusively animal diet.[1]"},{"year":"1928","event":"Vilhjalmur Stefansson's supervised meat-only year begins at Bellevue Hospital.[2]"},{"year":"2017","event":"Mikhaila Peterson creates the lion diet as an elimination protocol.[2]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Carnivore diet","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnivore_diet","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Carnivore diet","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Carnivore_diet","source":"Grokipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[{"title":"Carnivore diet","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Carnivore_diet","source":"Grokipedia","year":2025,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"BEEF LIVER (THE MOST POWERFUL FOOD ON EARTH)","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/beef-liver-the-most-powerful-food-on-earth.1555649/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20251017144324/https://looksmax.org/threads/beef-liver-the-most-powerful-food-on-earth.1555649/"},{"title":"THE STORY O